insert into documents (doc_type,title,source_url,doc_date,body) values ('news','Watermain Repair Scheduled on Park Lane Crescent - July 21, 2026 | Township of Ramara','https://www.ramara.ca/news/posts/watermain-repair-scheduled-on-park-lane-crescent-july-21-2026/','2026-07-21','Watermain Repair Scheduled on Park Lane Crescent - July 21, 2026 - Jul 20, 2026 Public Meetings and Notices The Ontario Clean Water Agency (OCWA), which operates and maintains the Township''s water system, has scheduled a watermain repair on Park Lane Crescent for Tuesday, July 21, 2026. The work will be completed by CC Underground. To complete this repair, some properties on Park Lane Crescent may experience a temporary water service interruption between 9 a.m. and approximately 5 p.m. Affected residents and property owners are being notified directly through hand-delivered notices. The Township appreciates residents'' patience and understanding while this necessary infrastructure repair is completed. Questions may be directed to the Infrastructure Department at 705-484-5374 ext. 285. Subscribe Back to News Search Contact Us Corporation of the Township of Ramara 2297 Highway 12, PO Box 130, Brechin, ON, L0K 1B0 T. 705-484-5374 E. ramara@ramara.ca Sign up for our eNewsletter Stay up to date on the Township''s activities, events, programs and operations by subscribing to have notifications sent directly to your inbox. Sign Up Today!'),('news','Ramara welcomes second physician to local medical practice | Township of Ramara','https://www.ramara.ca/news/posts/ramara-welcomes-second-physician-to-local-medical-practice/','2026-08-10','Ramara welcomes second physician to local medical practice Back to News Search Subscribe - Jul 22, 2026 Ramara, Ont. / July 22, 2026 – The Township of Ramara, in collaboration with the Couchiching Ontario Health Team (COHT) and the Orillia & Lake Country Physician Recruitment Committee (OLCPR), is pleased to announce that a second physician will be joining the Ramara Medical Centre in Brechin. Dr. Mehdi Dadashi, an experienced family physician with 20 years of clinical experience in family medicine and emergency care, will begin serving the Ramara community this fall. His arrival represents another important step in addressing local health-care needs and expanding access to primary care services for residents. “Welcoming Dr. Dadashi to Ramara is tremendous news for our community,” said Mayor Basil Clarke. “Together with Dr. Mo, Dr. Dadashi will help create a strong primary care network in Ramara, providing residents with greater access to family medicine and connected health services close to home. We are grateful to our partners at the Couchiching Ontario Health Team and the Orillia & Lake Country Physician Recruitment Committee for their continued support in helping bring physicians to our community.” Dr. Dadashi will join Dr. Anoushka Mohammadiankhorasani (Dr. Mo), who has now opened her practice at the Ramara Medical Centre in Brechin, and is connecting with patients. Together, the two physicians will help expand access to primary care services for residents and strengthen local health-care options closer to home. Dr. Dadashi brings 20 years of clinical experience in family medicine and emergency care. Throughout his career, he has provided comprehensive primary care to patients of all ages, including chronic disease management, preventive care, health promotion, and urgent medical care. He has also worked extensively in hospital and emergency settings managing acute and complex medical conditions. In addition to joining the Ramara Medical Centre, Dr. Dadashi will provide services at Orillia Soldiers’ Memorial Hospital. “Recruiting physicians to rural communities requires collaboration, innovation and a strong local commitment,” said Dr. Kim McIntosh, Primary Care Physician Lead for the Couchiching Ontario Health Team. “The addition of Dr. Dadashi further strengthens our local health-care system and enhances our ability to connect residents with comprehensive, team-based care close to home.” “I am honoured and excited to join the Ramara community and become part of its growing health-care team. Family medicine allows physicians to build lasting relationships with patients and families while supporting their health through every stage of life,” said Dr. Dadashi. “I have already experienced the warmth and welcoming spirit of the community and am grateful for the support shown by local leaders and health-care partners. I look forward to serving the residents of Ramara and working alongside my colleagues to provide accessible, compassionate, and high-quality care close to home.” The Ramara Medical Centre will operate as part of the Couchiching Ontario Health Team Primary Care Network, where local health-care providers work together to improve access to integrated, high-quality care. Through this partnership, patients benefit from access to a broader team of health-care professionals, including allied health supports provided through the Couchiching Family Health Team. How to Become a Patient: Priority will continue to be given to Ramara residents as part of this local physician recruitment initiative. Dr. Mo is now connecting with patients and will be conducting meet-and-greet appointments. Health Care Connect continues to actively match patients with Dr. Mo and will begin matching patients with Dr. Dadashi. Residents who have not yet registered and are interested in becoming a patient of Dr. Mo or Dr. Dadashi should register through Health Care Connect at: Phone: 1-800-445-1822 or call 811 Website: ontario.ca/HealthCareConnect Residents who are already registered with Health Care Connect do not need to register again and should monitor their email for further information. If your contact information has changed, please contact Health Care Connect to ensure your information is up to date. Residents who are already attached to a primary health care provider and are interested in becoming a patient of the new physicians in Ramara are encouraged to register with Health Care Connect. Patients do not need to leave their current physician to go on the Health Care Connect list. Individuals requiring assistance with the registration process may contact Emily at the Couchiching Ontario Health Team at 705-329-3649 ext. 241. For more information on health-care services in Ramara, visit ramara.ca/HealthCare . -30- Media Contact Melissa Gowanlock Manager of Communications & Community Experience 705-484-5374 ext. 322 mgowanlock@ramara.ca About the Orillia & Lake Country Physician Recruitment Committee Orillia & Lake Country Physician Recruitment Committee works to attract, retain and support family physicians and support specialist recruitment at Orillia Soldiers’ Memorial Hospital. OLCPR works alongside community partners, municipalities, economic development and clinical leads to support coordinated recruitment efforts. About the Couchiching Ontario Health Team The Couchiching Ontario Health Team (COHT) is a partnership of local health-care providers and organizations working together to plan, coordinate, and deliver seamless, integrated care for residents across the Couchiching region. As part of Ontario’s evolving health system, the COHT is focused on improving access to timely, high-quality care by connecting people to the right services, closer to home, while strengthening collaboration and communication across the health-care system. Dr. Mehdi Dadashi, an experienced family physician with 20 years of clinical experience in family medicine and emergency care, will join the Ramara Medical Centre and Orillia Soldiers’ Memorial Hospital this fall. Ramara Mayor Basil Clarke (left) and Ramara Deputy Mayor Keith Bell (right), with Dr. Mehdi Dadashi (centre) during a community tour of Ramara. Contact Us Corporation of the Township of Ramara 2297 Highway 12, PO Box 130, Brechin, ON, L0K 1B0 T. 705-484-5374 E. ramara@ramara.ca Sign up for our eNewsletter Stay up to date on the Township''s activities, events, programs and operations by subscribing to have notifications sent directly to your inbox. Sign Up Today!'),('news','Civic Holiday Schedule 2026 | Township of Ramara','https://www.ramara.ca/news/posts/civic-holiday-schedule-2026/','2026-08-10','Civic Holiday Schedule 2026 By Township of Ramara - Jul 24, 2026 Public Meetings and Notices The Township Administration Building will be closed for the Civic Holiday on Monday, August 3, 2026, reopening on Tuesday, August 4, 2026, at 9 a.m. During this time, online services remain available including: Report an infrastructure or bylaw concern View interactive mapping for trails, zoning and bylaw information Pay a bill Sign up for paperless billing Register for a recreation program And beyond See all online services at ramara.ca/OnlineServices . After-Hours Phone Numbers Canine Control - 705-623-7295 Roads, Municipal Water/Sewer - 705-484-5374, Option 9 Subscribe Back to News Search Contact Us Corporation of the Township of Ramara 2297 Highway 12, PO Box 130, Brechin, ON, L0K 1B0 T. 705-484-5374 E. ramara@ramara.ca Sign up for our eNewsletter Stay up to date on the Township''s activities, events, programs and operations by subscribing to have notifications sent directly to your inbox. Sign Up Today!'),('news','Wastewater Treatment Facility Project 202 Construction Update - July 29, 2026 | Township of Ramara','https://www.ramara.ca/news/posts/wastewater-treatment-facility-project-202-construction-update-july-29-2026/','2026-07-29','Wastewater Treatment Facility Project 202 Construction Update - July 29, 2026 - Jul 29, 2026 Public Meetings and Notices An update has been issued regarding the Wastewater Treatment Facility Project 202. It includes a summary of completed work, upcoming activities, traffic impacts, and recent construction photos. Please read the full notice and view the latest project photos for all details. Subscribe Back to News Search Contact Us Corporation of the Township of Ramara 2297 Highway 12, PO Box 130, Brechin, ON, L0K 1B0 T. 705-484-5374 E. ramara@ramara.ca Sign up for our eNewsletter Stay up to date on the Township''s activities, events, programs and operations by subscribing to have notifications sent directly to your inbox. Sign Up Today!'),('news','Health Care Connect Registration Event Coming to Ramara Medical Centre - August 5, 2026 | Township of Ramara','https://www.ramara.ca/news/posts/health-care-connect-registration-event-coming-to-ramara-medical-centre-august-5-2026/','2026-08-05','Health Care Connect Registration Event Coming to Ramara Medical Centre - August 5, 2026 Back to News Search Subscribe - Jul 30, 2026 Public Meetings and Notices The Township of Ramara is pleased to share that the Couchiching Ontario Health Team (COHT) is hosting an in-person Health Care Connect registration event to help eligible Ramara residents connect with primary care services. Residents who do not currently have a local family doctor or nurse practitioner are invited to attend and receive assistance registering with Health Care Connect, Ontario''s centralized patient registration program. With new physicians joining the Ramara Medical Centre, registering with Health Care Connect is the first step toward being connected with a local primary care provider. As part of this physician recruitment initiative, priority will continue to be given to Ramara residents. What: Health Care Connect In-Person Registration Event Date: Wednesday, Aug. 5, 2026 Time: 2 to 6 p.m. Location: Ramara Medical Centre 3242 Ramara Road 47 Brechin, ON Please Bring Residents attending the event must bring a valid Ontario Health Card showing their current address, as this is required to complete registration. Who Should Attend? This event is intended for residents who: Do not currently have a local family doctor or nurse practitioner and wish to register with Health Care Connect. Currently have a primary care provider but are interested in becoming a patient of one of the new physicians in Ramara. You do not need to leave your current provider to register with Health Care Connect. Residents who are already registered with Health Care Connect do not need to register again. They should continue to monitor their email for updates. If your contact information has changed, please contact Health Care Connect to ensure your information is current. Can''t Attend? If you are unable to attend the registration event, you can still register with Health Care Connect: Online: ontario.ca/HealthCareConnect By phone: 1-800-445-1822 If you need assistance with the registration process, please contact Emily at 705-329-3649 ext. 241. The Township of Ramara thanks the Couchiching Ontario Health Team and the Orillia & Lake Country Physician Recruitment Committee for their continued partnership and commitment to improving access to primary care for Ramara residents. Learn More About Ramara''s New Doctors Contact Us Corporation of the Township of Ramara 2297 Highway 12, PO Box 130, Brechin, ON, L0K 1B0 T. 705-484-5374 E. ramara@ramara.ca Sign up for our eNewsletter Stay up to date on the Township''s activities, events, programs and operations by subscribing to have notifications sent directly to your inbox. Sign Up Today!'),('news','Scheduled Watermain Repair and Temporary Water Service Interruption - Wednesday, August 5, 2026','https://www.ramara.ca/news/posts/scheduled-watermain-repair-and-temporary-water-service-interruption-wednesday-august-5-2026/','2026-08-05','Scheduled Watermain Repair and Temporary Water Service Interruption - Wednesday, August 5, 2026 - Jul 31, 2026 Public Meetings and Notices Poplar Crescent and Willow Crescent Wednesday, August 5, 2026 The Township''s Operating Authority has identified a leaking watermain valve on Poplar Crescent in Lagoon City. Repairs to the distribution system are scheduled for Wednesday, August 5, 2026. Crews will begin mobilizing and excavating at 8:00 a.m. Service Impact Area The repair will require a temporary watermain shutdown affecting: Properties from 21 Poplar Crescent to 41 Poplar Crescent All properties on Willow Crescent Residents within the affected service area will receive a hand-delivered notice prior to the schedule repair with details regarding the anticipated water service interruption and recommended preparations. Watermain Disinfection and Flushing Following completion of the repair, the repaired section of watermain will be cleaned, disinfected and flushed in accordance with provincial drinking water requirements before being returned to service. Residents in the area may experience temporary discoloured water following the flushing activities. If this occurs, run a cold water tap until the water runs clear. The Township appreciates the patience and cooperation of its residents as this necessary infrastructure work is completed. Please note: The work is weather dependent. If the repair is delayed due to weather or unforeseen circumstances, the Township will communicate any schedule changes through its website and social media channels. For additional information, please contact the Infrastructure Department at 705-484-5374 ext. 285. Affected Area - Scheduled Watermain Repair Wednesday, August 5, 2026 Subscribe Back to News Search Contact Us Corporation of the Township of Ramara 2297 Highway 12, PO Box 130, Brechin, ON, L0K 1B0 T. 705-484-5374 E. ramara@ramara.ca Sign up for our eNewsletter Stay up to date on the Township''s activities, events, programs and operations by subscribing to have notifications sent directly to your inbox. Sign Up Today!') on conflict (source_url) do nothing;